{"term":"stereotype","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cb6e8d1ee9fb9ab427","definition":"A conventional, formulaic, and often oversimplified or exaggerated conception, opinion, or image of (a person or a group of people).","example":"Not all Zumbetonians wear plimsolls. That's just a stereotype.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:908a0028fa7aa063a8","definition":"A person who is regarded as embodying or conforming to a set image or type.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cdc8f37854683ca39e","definition":"A metal printing plate cast from a matrix moulded from a raised printing surface.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["cliché"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c