.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6b82acfbcae15e521e","definition":"To print from a stereotype.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer","stereotypable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e152ad54e6d3c68b12","definition":"To make firm or permanent; to fix.","example":"Powerful causes tending to stereotype and aggravate the poverty of old conditions.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer","stereotypable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2c23c0a3a553d7dd7e","definition":"Of an edition: printed in stereotype.","example":"At the present Epoch (1800), the art of Printing is become rather retrograde; or we should not hear so much of Stereotype editions. Surely the use and very principle of the invention of Printing, is to have the types moveable!","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer","stereotypable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a04dc0a29b53884e65","definition":"Synonym of stereotyped.","example":"It is an ingenious expression which I owe to you, sir, that the manners of the East are as it were stereotype. Ahhough I do not conceive that they are quite so strongly marked, yet, to make my idea understood, I would say that they are like the last impressions taken from a copper-plate engraving, where the whole of the subject to be represented is made out, although parts of it from much use have been obliterated.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["stereotyped"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, rare","register":"figuratively, rare","wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer","stereotypable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈstɛ.ɹi.əˌtaɪp/"},"wordFamily":["counterstereotype","stereotyper","cybertype","metastereotype","stereotype tax","stereotype threat","stereotypic","stereotypical","stereotypist","stereotypographer","stereotypable"]}